menu "WB DIY firmware"

choice WB_MODBUS_ROLE
    prompt "Modbus role"
    default WB_MODBUS_ROLE_SLAVE
    help
        What this firmware does with Modbus, decided once at BUILD time for the whole
        device. It is not a runtime setting: the roles pull in different code, and the
        point of "none" is that the Modbus stack is not linked at all.

        Build it from the Makefile with MB_ROLE=<slave|master|none>, e.g.
        `make MB_ROLE=master build-idf-project`; each role writes its own sdkconfig, so
        switching back and forth cannot leave a stale configuration behind.

config WB_MODBUS_ROLE_SLAVE
    bool "slave - Modbus RTU on both RS-485 ports and a Modbus TCP server"
    help
        The default, and the behaviour this firmware has always had. Both RS-485 ports
        answer as Modbus RTU slaves and the Modbus TCP server runs; all three share one
        unit id (mb_slave_id), one TCP port setting (mb_tcp_port) and one register map
        (main/mb_slave/mb_registers.c).

        Modbus TCP belongs to this role and to no other.

config WB_MODBUS_ROLE_MASTER
    bool "master - poll other devices on both RS-485 ports"
    help
        The device is the master on both RS-485 buses: main/mb_master/ brings up one
        Modbus RTU master per port and offers a blocking request API the application
        calls from its own task. There is no Modbus TCP and no slave register store in
        this role, so mb_slave_id and mb_tcp_port do not exist either.

config WB_MODBUS_ROLE_NONE
    bool "none - no Modbus at all"
    help
        Neither main/mb_slave/ nor main/mb_master/ is compiled and nothing references
        esp-modbus, so the whole Modbus stack drops out of the image (~82 KB of flash).
        Everything else - the web UI, the settings API, the RS-485 transceiver control,
        the factory test - keeps working.

        No UART driver is installed on either RS-485 port, so nothing is transmitted and
        nothing is received. The two transceivers are NOT simply left alone, though: with
        no UART to drive their direction lines, app_main parks both DE/RE pins LOW once at
        boot, so each transceiver sits in receive and cannot hold a shared bus. The
        485_tx_dis_N settings stay in the API but have nothing to apply to in this role.

endchoice

endmenu
